{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872617-need-help-figuring-this-out-does-fire-damage-ignore-regular-armor","id":872617,"title":"Need help figuring this out, Does fire damage ignore regular armor.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-23T13:37:34-07:00","id":872617,"title":"Need help figuring this out, Does fire damage ignore regular armor.","content":"We had an explosion pure fire damage did, 9-10 aggravated and a player is disputing saying he was wearing 2/0 armor does it block fire aggravated damage which is a kindred bane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T13:55:17-07:00","id":872626,"title":"","content":"1) Is he wearing an anti-bomb armor?<br /> <br /> 2) Is the explosion purely incendiary?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T13:57:19-07:00","id":872628,"title":"","content":"He's wearing 2/0 hard leather and its an incendiary blast bomb with pressure that took out a nearby warehouse as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T14:02:58-07:00","id":872633,"title":"","content":"Nah, that doesn't help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T14:03:04-07:00","id":872634,"title":"","content":"In 2E (haven't checked for 1E) RAW just says that General Armor applies to all attacks, starting with the most damaging type (Agg, Lethal, Bashing). I can't find any text in 2E Requiem or 2E WoD that says Explosion Damage is treated differently. <br /> <br /> Now - maybe you could rule that the Explosion is actually more an environmental hardship than an attack, so it ignores armor, but I'd be a little salty about that if I were a player. Downgrading 9-10 aggravated damage to 7-8 aggravated damage is still going to kill the average Kindred without Resilience, and leave the rest pretty bad off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T14:05:28-07:00","id":872636,"title":"","content":"So the blast came and our gm did a secondary roll, the player saying that all damage in 2E comes at -1 and his armor would abosrb -2 agqainst the Kindred bane of fire","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T14:54:13-07:00","id":872656,"title":"","content":"Well, if the explosion really is &quot;pure fire damage&quot; then it's probably treated the same way as the flamethrower in the Hurt Locker equipment appendix preview. <i>&quot;Armor only helps if it's some kind of flame-resistant suit.&quot; </i>10 damage of &quot;pure fire&quot; seems a bit excessive, but it's hard to judge the fairness of a situation in a vacuum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T15:05:48-07:00","id":872661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chaos965</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872617-need-help-figuring-this-out-does-fire-damage-ignore-regular-armor?p=872636#post872636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the blast came and our gm did a secondary roll, the player saying that all damage in 2E comes at -1 and his armor would abosrb -2 agqainst the Kindred bane of fire</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not sure what he means by all damage comes in at (-1), unless he's talking about the fact that most forms of Lethal damage are automatically downgraded to Bashing for Kindred. But that doesn't lower the amount of damage taken, only the type. Because Fire is a Bane means that rather than suffering Lethal Damage like a mortal would, a vampire would instead take Aggravated Damage. Again, that's only a change in type.<br /> <br /> Also technically, pure fire at the hardest/hottest levels is limited to burning you for 6 Aggravated Damage per turn of exposure. That's a Vampire caught in a raging phosphorus fire. If the damage is treated as burning and not an 'attack'; then yeah, I'd say it's fair to rule armor doesn't effect that. But then I'd quibble with the 9-10 damage in one go.<br /> <br /> Most generic explosions assume there is also impact/concussion/shrapnel damage being thrown around, which general armor <i>should</i> apply to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T15:30:57-07:00","id":872677,"title":"","content":"Actually it says general armor reduces the damage by one point <i>per point of armor.</i> (God Machine Chronicle p. 205) not that he gets an additional 1 plus another 2 for the rating of hard leather. The description for general armor says it also only applies to normal or firearms attacks. Armor, in most cases, does not block aggravated damage either since it ignores Durability rating on equipment. If there's absolutely no incidental damage from debris from the explosion which could destroy the armor, the armor could still be be obliterated by the force damage from the explosion before fire enters the equation. <br /> Honestly it's still up to whoever is adjudicating the scenario since I've no idea on how equipment durability is handled and whether or not mundane things auto downgrade aggravated damage from mystical sources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T15:54:04-07:00","id":872694,"title":"","content":"I think the -1 to all damage the player is quoting is the fast and dirty guidelines for converting weapon damage bonuses from 1st to 2nd edition, not an innate damage reduction in general. They probably used an explosive from 1st edition as a starting point to decide how much damage was inflicted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T17:11:32-07:00","id":872745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872617-need-help-figuring-this-out-does-fire-damage-ignore-regular-armor?p=872661#post872661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also technically, pure fire at the hardest/hottest levels is limited to burning you for 6 Aggravated Damage per turn of exposure. That's a Vampire caught in a raging phosphorus fire. If the damage is treated as burning and not an 'attack'; then yeah, I'd say it's fair to rule armor doesn't effect that. But then I'd quibble with the 9-10 damage in one go.<br /> <br /> Most generic explosions assume there is also impact/concussion/shrapnel damage being thrown around, which general armor <i>should</i> apply to.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. If the attack is doing more than 6 damage, it's not &quot;pure&quot; fire. Some of that is coming from the force of the explosion, and/or shrapnel. The armor shouldn't apply against the burning (6 agg), but it should apply against the remaining 3 damage, which should probably be lethal unless the character is at ground zero. Either way, that's going to be downgraded by the vampire template, so the total should be 6 agg from burning and 1 bashing from the explosion (or 1 lethal if the character is at ground zero).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}